      I went to business school to move closer to product and technology, and to work where technical execution meets the customer and the business. Over the past year I've been building and deploying AI, including production LLM agents now in daily use. I'm most useful translating between engineers, customers, and executives, and turning messy problems into working systems.
    </p>
    <p>
      My engineering background isn't a past life, it's the edge. I understand technical systems and real-world operations, not just software abstractions.
    </p>
    <p>
